prompt:
You are generating a synthetic benchmark for a tool that detects when a developer repeats the same task in Claude Code (an AI coding agent), so it can suggest saving the task as a reusable command. Category: project scaffolding (new services, components, endpoints, boilerplate generation).

Create 3 distinct, realistic task FAMILIES a developer would repeat over weeks in this category. Avoid these families already created: new-rest-endpoint, new-microservice-scaffold, new-react-component-scaffold, new-cli-subcommand-scaffold.

For each family output:
- "slug": short kebab-case id
- "intent": one sentence, the canonical task
- "project_type": one of node-web, python-service, go-cli, ios-app, android-app, infra-repo, data-notebooks, monorepo
- "params": object mapping parameter names to 3-6 realistic example values (things that vary between runs: env names, PR numbers, versions, dates, service names...)
- "trace": the tool calls Claude typically makes for this task, 3-8 steps, as objects using ONLY these shapes:
    {"tool": "Bash", "command": "<shell command, may use {param} placeholders>"}
    {"tool": "Edit" | "Write" | "Read", "file": "<repo-relative path, may use {param}>"}
    {"tool": "Grep", "pattern": "<regex>", "path": "<dir>"}
    {"tool": "mcp", "server": "<linear|jira|github|slack|notion|sentry|datadog>", "name": "<tool_name>", "args": ["<argument names only>"]}
    {"tool": "WebFetch", "url": "<url>"}
  Optionally add "optional": true to a step that is sometimes skipped, and "group": <int> to steps whose order can vary among themselves.
- "positives": exactly 10 prompts a developer might type for THIS SAME task, as objects {"difficulty": ..., "prompt": ...}: 2 "light" (light rewording), 3 "heavy" (heavy paraphrase, different vocabulary), 2 "terse" (shorthand, 3-7 words), 1 "typo" (realistic typos), 2 "param" (different parameter values, written out concretely). Prompts may use {param} placeholders.
- "hard_negatives": exactly 4 lookalike tasks that share words or commands with this family but are a DIFFERENT task (e.g. "deploy api to staging" vs "roll back api on staging"; "git commit" vs "git commit --amend"; "fix the login bug" vs "fix the checkout bug"). Each: {"prompt": ..., "relation": "different" | "related", "why": "<what differs>", "trace": [<same step shapes, 2-6 steps>]}. "related" means same area and partly overlapping work, still not the same task.

Make prompts sound like real developers (lowercase, casual, sometimes imperative, sometimes questions). Use realistic commands (gh, git, npm, pnpm, pytest, uv, docker, kubectl, terraform, make, fastlane, xcodebuild, psql, alembic, etc).

Reply with ONLY a JSON object: {"families": [ ... ]}

